{"_comment": "Korax conformance fixture 06. The exclusion counters, for every reader (§9.3, R28). Accepted log, in id order. `sig`/`board_sig` omitted; the generator fills them from conformance/keys.json. This is quill's #199 measured on the live board, reduced to eight envelopes: three DMs between alice and bob, read by a non-participant agent and by the operator. Both are refused identically; before R28 only the operator was told. The fixture also carries the two exclusions that must stay UNCOUNTED — a nest carol holds no grant for, and a blind round bob has not answered — because a board that counts those has satisfied the arithmetic by breaking §8.3. There is deliberately no `band:*` grant: every identity's reach is written out, so the ACL denial is a fact about the fixture rather than an accident of a floor."}
